    {
      "id": "stroke-control-instructions",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Stroke Control Sketch",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -2060,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "guided-by",
          "key": "guided-by",
          "label": "guided by",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "role": "relationship",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "reference"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "relationship"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "stroke-control"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Stroke Control (sketch)\n\nA graph template, `templates/stroke-control`. Names are illustrative.\n\n## It declares\n\n- Five Properties: `color` (text, `#6d28d9`), `width` (number, `8`), `opacity` (number, `1`), `dash` (text, `solid`), `enabled` (boolean, `true`). Each announces `property.changed`.\n- A default view that shows the swatch and the values, and a summary and icon that show the swatch.\n\n## It keeps itself current\n\n- One Handler for any Property changed, calling one Method that re-renders the swatch and writes it into the exposed views.\n- The Method declares exactly those views as its effects, like the Edge Class template's Method.\n\n## It is consumed through a Bridge\n\n- An export Bridge exposes the five Properties' events.\n- The Edge Class template imports the control. Each stroke is one instance, and its refresh Handler listens to the class through the Bridge.\n\n## Not in scope\n\nArrows, gradients, animation and glow. The control is one paint layer, and the Edge Class template still owns route, arrows and the stack order."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        }
      },
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
