      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "A Stroke Is a Control Graph",
        "statement": "The stroke widget should be a small graph of its own, not a bag of values on one node. Color, width, opacity, dash and enabled become real Properties that each announce property.changed. A swatch view keeps itself current through the same Handler and Method pattern the Edge Class template already uses. An export Bridge exposes the control's events, and the Edge Class template consumes each stroke through a Bridge. Editing an edge class then means editing composed controls, live.",
        "status": "framed",
        "confidence": "unproven",
        "notes": "Builds on the Edge Class template (github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/edge-class-template/root.node), where Property and stroke changes already refresh the exposed views through class-scoped Handlers, and on the Bridge Editor idea (github://mikemartinez1974/public/ideas/bridge-editor/root.node), which is where a control's events would be exposed.",
        "definitionKey": "idea",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea.node-class.node",
