          "portId": "affects"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "A Stroke Is Values on One Node",
        "statement": "Today a stroke is a field node bound to the edge-class-stroke class, with color, width, opacity, dash and enabled as raw data keys. It announces one coarse node.changed event that lists which keys changed, so nothing can react to one setting on its own. No setting has its own type, access or default, and the editor is a generic form. The control also cannot be reused: it is welded to the Edge Class template that happens to contain it.",
        "impact": "The edge class settings editor, the thing the template previews, is the weakest editor in the graph. Every new control (a color, a paint stack, an arrow) would repeat the same shortcut.",
        "urgency": "high",
        "definitionKey": "idea-problem",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "idea-problem",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/idea-template/classes/nodes/idea-problem.node-class.node",
