      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "What exists today",
        "findings": "A stroke is a field node bound to the edge-class-stroke class and announces node.changed with the keys that changed. A Handler can listen to one node or to every node of a class, and a class can declare events that its instances inherit. The Edge Class template refreshes its three exposed views from Property and stroke changes through three Handlers and one Method that writes stored SVG. Bridges expose and consume events one node at a time only, and their Events UI has only just been given its own section in the Properties panel.",
        "sourceUrl": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/edge-class-template/root.node",
        "sourceType": "prototype",
        "definitionKey": "idea-research",
