      "data": {
        "title": "Too much machinery for a small control",
        "description": "A graph, a Bridge, a Handler and a Method per stroke is heavy for five values. Several strokes multiply the Bridges, and if class-scoped events cannot cross Bridges cleanly the consumer becomes fragile.",
        "likelihood": "medium",
        "impact": "high",
        "mitigation": "Prove one instance end to end before generalizing, and decide the class-scoped Bridge behavior first because everything else depends on it. If it stays heavy, the alternative remains available.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-risk",
